rm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $‖v‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2+5\\cdot (3\\cdot 3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+45} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-141167/selection/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078" :answer/id #uuid "df89db0b-eeef-5618-8765-65957c5d75b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141167/selection/d18a8dda3b8d65edd15eaec58978ca4092dbb278a54eb8bcb12a2dd65a77d732" :answer/id #uuid "8c41e0f4-705a-56bd-b39a-8abe336523f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141167/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" :answer/id #uuid "ac47e7cf-caaa-5f81-81a8-c53bd757c1dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141167/selection/e59e169232e16e8d4fc95e4d14f7ebab8f0ea66430d2fabd4381548437f83344" :answer/id #uuid "12d336ee-0d17-540f-8180-c981b7c25631" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141167/selection/539a2a78543f2770355c2dd0e8aba9dc4c38c69e2526206b8cac8c4c60782484" :answer/id #uuid "e4758cb0-61fb-5fa9-88b1-6e7f6d2326dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141167/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2cd76808-9a8b-58eb-9a64-8f4ac3af00d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141167/selection/539a2a78543f2770355c2dd0e8aba9dc4c38c69e2526206b8cac8c4c60782484" :answer-field/choices ["q-141167/selection/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078" "q-141167/selection/d18a8dda3b8d65edd15eaec58978ca4092dbb278a54eb8bcb12a2dd65a77d732" "q-141167/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" "q-141167/selection/e59e169232e16e8d4fc95e4d14f7ebab8f0ea66430d2fabd4381548437f83344" "q-141167/selection/539a2a78543f2770355c2dd0e8aba9dc4c38c69e2526206b8cac8c4c60782484"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141167" :question/id #uuid "2cfd7234-83ad-57e9-960b-f838a9b42ca8" :question/math-academy-id "q-141167" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=2-t+{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=2-t+{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=2,\\,p(2)=4,\\,p(3)=8.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{84} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141167/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141167"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97425/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "d43bde1b-fa03-5c0a-aa29-f4f6493c0650" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97425/selection/d253ac0ac20b641e12f953f9412aa9f9d95729120756fea738c6358f9fcb04d9" :answer/id #uuid "1d6e4c7e-42