ner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=5-3t,$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(0)=5,\\,p(2)=-1,\\,p(3)=-4.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(0)p(0)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(0)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{42}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97425/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97425"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-97420"] :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(0)y(0)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=4-2t+{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=4-2t+{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(0)=4,\\,p(2)=4,\\,p(3)=7.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(0)p(0)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(0)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(4)^{2}+(7)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16+49} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-97422/selection/5371f7c0b0dcb7971e259333187268b3f161f844a21da0bac5a59ac2c4f7743f" :answer/id #uuid "aefb5a38-b4d0-556c-a547-8ad1308074f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97422/selection/219833e7