^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=4-{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=3,\\,p(0)=4,\\,p(-1)=3.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(0)p(0)+p(-1)p(-1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(0)]^{2}+[p(-1)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(4)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97422/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97422"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97418/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "2ffde8f9-ecbe-50f1-99d4-3a8686ff4281" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97418/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer/id #uuid "0f1d2ff6-930f-5906-99eb-91e73481eb08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97418/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "5c7c0d23-c009-5c2a-92f9-d3ed2ce3e038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97418/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "8bd201b4-faf6-5032-9249-1454a6d3162d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97418/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "cc052681-1ae2-59db-85f9-9af44265211a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97418/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9826e7c-0174-5202-93b2-53300ad5735a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97418/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-97418/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-97418/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" "q-97418/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-97418/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-97418/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97418" :question/id #uuid "4e07ea74-65b4-594e-914e-fe1b3c0f9704" :question/math-academy-id "q-97418" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(0)y(0)+x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=2+t-{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=2+t-{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(0)=2,\\,p(1)=2,\\,p(2)=0.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(0)p(0)+p(1)p(1)+p(2)p(2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(0)]^{2}+[p(1)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97418/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97418"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validat