920" :question/id #uuid "6e5ddf58-998d-561f-b859-a4149f98cf8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-43920" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=2t+\\sqrt{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t+\\sqrt{t})^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+4t\\sqrt{t}+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4{t}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{8{t}^{2}\\sqrt{t}}{5}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{8}{5}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{103}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{\\frac{103}{30}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-43920/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43920"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141171/selection/658e13114e50404bfb966982d9e3eef2d6dc844854183bdfac088c45d3652b1c" :answer/id #uuid "314dc21b-8871-5df2-a10f-d67e3bed48fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2\\pi +1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141171/selection/29c1fe83afe5deb064e80d2eb0c474b3dc232f9db8109239bf6710e4dd7f189d" :answer/id #uuid "9b143890-0503-5b24-8531-6e85acf23ee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2\\pi +2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141171/selection/d65ab5694d946eb620bfc4935477bffe2aca3faa7b67a11968938fabb43d0823" :answer/id #uuid "a1c66ed9-f5a7-5e46-b119-fe80c0508e4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141171/selection/4d558e7d0657a79eeebdee9627d1d0e020a904611d9143bb6e0dfa1c581ad9ad" :answer/id #uuid "9bdb1a46-0d13-58b3-84ac-263992a26deb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141171/selection/8f3ef73b7999870c68e02c54e14bf59d32e0c05408243c9952a057bf19f6acf5" :answer/id #uuid "83c6089a-5085-5afa-9420-c8c743c14463" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141171/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e0e9478-9f06-55a6-a86b-6a58136206e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141171/selection/d65ab5694d946eb620bfc4935477bffe2aca3faa7b67a11968938fabb43d0823" :answer-field/choices ["q-141171/selection/658e13114e50404bfb966982d9e3eef2d6dc844854183bdfac088c45d3652b1c" "q-141171/selection/29c1fe83afe5deb064e80d2eb0c474b3dc232f9db8109239bf6710e4dd7f189d" "q-141171/selection/d65ab5694d946eb620bfc4935477bffe2aca3faa7b67a11968938fabb43d0823" "q-141171/selection/4d558e7d0657a79eeebdee9627d1d0e020a904611d9143bb6e0dfa1c581ad9ad" "q-141171/selection/8f3ef73b7999870c68e02c54e14bf59d32e0c05408243c9952a057bf19f6acf5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141171" :question/id #uuid "76a38372-c4e4-54ba-9d14-0563306ec42c" :question/math-academy-id "q-141171" :question/problem "Let $V=C[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\,{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\,({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2}){|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\pi +\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi }{2})-((-\\pi )+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2\\pi )}{2}) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we made use of the trigonometric identities\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1\\,\\text{and}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFinally then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖f(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{2\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141171/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141171"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141170/selection/380766111bded0cb28a25a817a0d5982bebd55701d775263f61123ddb008d105" :answer/id #uuid "ba06921c-997b-516d-8291-540cf4b031aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141170/selection/a9e249a39e82f48ded5fb654b4049c08b472396d246820b51dfa83b8738ccf06" :answer/id #uuid "826dff1e-eda2-541a-bfbc-fb1f4f6f09f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141170/selection/d6351af074d3a54f1bd8a4d557a5d381858a6a5d5650ac4841094612f6165f95" :answer/id #uuid "68795571-006f-58aa-ae3f-9ce848f8b9a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141170/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "380a9d83-dd4c-5f2e-beac-af7ddc86f847" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141170/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "8cc2c4c9-5baf-5a56-8da9-d4b1cfbe8957" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141170/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ceeabe5-4f09-5832-9388-27a782316d67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141170/selection/a9e249a39e82f48ded5fb654b4049c08b472396d246820b51dfa83b8738ccf06" :answer-field/choices ["q-141170/selection/380766111bded0cb28a25a817a0d5982bebd55701d775263f61123ddb008d105" "q-141170/selection/a9e249a39e82f48ded5fb654b4049c08b472396d246820b51dfa83b8738ccf06" "q-141170/selection/d6351af074d3a54f1bd8a4d557a5d381858a6a5d5650ac4841094612f6165f95" "q-141170/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-141170/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141170" :question/id #uuid "d0f46084-f755-54b3-bb66-e1e926747894" :question/math-academy-id "q-141170" :question/problem "Let $V=C[-1,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-1,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=1-t.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(1-t)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{2}-2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-{t}^{2}+t)|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-1+1)-(\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}-(-1)^{2}+(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{3}}=2\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141170/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141170"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-43927/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "57d39f7f-060a-54db-9e76-bcdf3a628788" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43927/selection/ed480161c278cf263b7506697b7b27c19b2594926ada6527945331e6eb5a4b3b" :answer/id #uuid "68652c2d-3c60-5d33-b3db-3db6612a3308" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43927/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "f8f94225-f841-503b-b628-9340e642f28a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43927/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" :answer/id #uuid "1024d53f-3bae-5f03-8e5f-d9ed1a48f2ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43927/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "47a7750a-a97e-577f-aa2e-ecd07eafc536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43927/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "acac7b88-b62d-5bbc-8154-74db303a3fff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-43927/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" :answer-field/choices ["q-43927/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-43927/selection/ed480161c278cf263b7506697b7b27c19b2594926ada6527945331e6eb5a4b3b" "q-43927/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" "q-43927/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" "q-43927/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-43927" :question/id #uuid "51d00b91-6609-5dca-af51-01db0863a49f" :question/math-academy-id "q-43927" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=3t+1.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3t+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9{t}^{2}+6t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(3{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+t)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3+3+1 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{7}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-43927/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43927"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97712/selection/8673add8fa601a4f14f69232b6be726b1df0e457e68b98f11200ff918b74082d" :answer/id #uuid "a7cf3cb0-2652-5d0b-8b77-07ad50054bdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97712/selection/74a3fff9c1e8415bd116d4946d8988663b0da25924809d8aefd229691fad11bd" :answer/id #uuid "01bc5cd8-5240-5e22-9ec2-bbe3e86b6cef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3\\pi +5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97712/selection/ef67a76cbb1960f5723772c0b513a580d705036a1dc342a